WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.270
A man of many names and just as many faces,
with one characteristic, unsettlingly wide

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:11.420
smile, Doctor Alto Clef has long been one
of the SCP Foundation’s most valuable researchers.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.270
Granted, he also happens to be their most
infamous and would almost take the title of

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.280
their strangest member of personnel.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.439
In fact, Clef might be tied for the title
of strangest with one other researcher who

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:25.670
was literally turned into a dog.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.880
But what does an average day look like for
the so-called Ukulele Man?

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.880
Surely somebody of Clef’s reputation as
a violent, unpredictable and enigmatic figure

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.640
doesn’t just punch the clock at the Foundation
and settle for a boring day filing paperwork.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.780
Well, if you’ve ever wondered what his normal
schedule might look like, then luckily, we’ve

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.540
prepared a look at a Day in the Life of Doctor
Alto Clef.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.960
6:00 AM
Rising at an hour most ordinary people would

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.640
consider absurdly early, Alto Clef seemingly
begins his day much like the rest of us.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.000
He sits up in bed, gets to his feet and washes
himself thoroughly to prepare for the day

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
ahead.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
In order to make the most effective use of
this time in the morning, despite being up

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.830
at the break of dawn, Clef likes to complete
smaller, trivial tasks in regard to his personal

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.350
health hygiene.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.650
Although it does little to change the unsettling
aura that follows him around, never let it

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:23.980
be said that Doctor Clef doesn’t take meticulous
care of himself – perhaps even to neurotic

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:24.980
degree.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.780
He’ll begin with exercise, usually trying
to break his record for number of pull ups

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.070
and push ups he can complete in a short amount
of time.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.070
If he finds his face is a little puffy first
thing in the morning, he’ll instead don

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.650
an ice pack while doing stomach crunches.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:39.730
His record for those?

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.960
A thousand in a row… and counting.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.260
Clef will then follow this up with showering,
using the time under the water to meditate.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:52.850
It seems odd for someone known for his various
acts of great violence, but even Alto Clef

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.650
can take a moment for calm, reflective mediation.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:01.820
Then, while showering, he moves on to the
application of a deep pore cleansing lotion,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.430
and is particularly fond of his honey almond
body scrub.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.200
Then, exiting and applying a herb-mint face
mask – which he leaves on for ten minutes

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.430
as part of his routine – Doctor Clef engages
in his strangest morning activity.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.990
While standing in front of the mirror in his
private quarters, he will just… stare at

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.990
himself.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:25.160
It’s certainly an odd action, especially
spending such a specific allotment of time

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.319
doing so.

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:30.319
But even more unusual is how he seems to practice
smiling…

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:34.420
Whenever photographed, Doctor Alto Clef’s
face is always bizarrely replaced with that

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.780
of a random animal or object.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.760
Each time, the animal face will be sporting
a wide, almost abnormal grin; the same expression

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.680
Clef practices in the mirror each morning.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.209
It is still unknown whether the concealment
of his face to photography is an active or

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.970
passive ability Doctor Clef possesses, whether
he does it on purpose or can’t help it.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.680
8:00 AM
Breakfast is usually a meal Clef skips; instead

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.790
of cereal or even a healthy piece of fruit,
every morning he’ll sustain himself on more

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:06.260
vitamins than any normal human being would
take in a week.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.310
We do not recommend trying this at home!

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.530
Being awake so early affords Doctor Clef the
luxury of a few moments’ downtime before

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.360
the beginning of a long working day at the
SCP Foundation.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.209
Part of Alto Clef’s infamous reputation
is he is known to be something of a weapons

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:28.400
enthusiast, and often acts as a go-to executioner
when the Foundation need an anomaly ‘taken

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.400
care of’.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.760
As a result, and as it pertains to his job,
during Clef’s morning downtime he familiarises

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:39.620
himself with one of his favorite armament
publications Guns, Guns and Oh Look, More

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:40.709
Guns!

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:46.019
Although how he acquires these magazines and
indeed who actually publishes them is unknown.

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:50.930
Alternatively, he will request SCP Archive
files to be delivered to his quarters so he

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.230
can read up on any anomalies the Foundation
has encountered that might have the potential

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.680
to be weaponized.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.930
Of course, this is more just a hobby, not
something Clef would actually attempt… unless

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.120
asked to.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.870
But speaking of having things delivered to
his room, it is normally around this time

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.970
of the morning that a frightened member of
D Class is sent to knock on Doctor Clef’s

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:11.970
door.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.650
Now this too seems rather odd.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:19.329
The role of D Class is to be expendable, usually
as human test subjects for anomalies, placed

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:23.570
in dangerous situations so as not to cost
the lives of Foundation personnel.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:28.479
Then, of course, knocking on the door to Alto
Clef’s quarters is potentially a rather

00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:30.300
dangerous situation.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.160
It's hard to know for certain if the D Class
sent to hand deliver Doctor Clef’s daily

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.539
itinerary will survive the encounter.

00:04:36.539 --> 00:04:42.050
Given his renowned unpredictability, it usually
ends up being a fifty-fifty coin toss.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.490
Of course, it does beg the question, why don’t
the Foundation just send Clef an email to

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:49.250
notify him what anomaly he’ll be ‘decommissioning’.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.669
But, then again, being handed a paper itinerary
by a D Class was something that Clef himself

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:55.669
requested.

00:04:55.669 --> 00:04:58.550
10:00 AM
By late morning, Alto has normally finished

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.889
cleaning up whatever was left of his ill-fated
D Class messenger; unless he was in the mood

00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:03.889
to spare them.

00:05:03.889 --> 00:05:09.120
Sure, killing them certainly seemed an excessive
practice to engage in, but Clef had seemingly

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.889
convinced the Foundation that it was ‘necessary’
for him to function.

00:05:12.889 --> 00:05:17.699
It’s obvious that this diabolical doctor
is well aware of his usefulness to the Foundation.

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:23.060
He has long proven himself to be highly proficient
at dispatching dangerous anomalies with ease,

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.180
so it’s likely the Foundation fulfills his
bloodthirsty requests thanks to that factor.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:31.930
After all, they would hardly be likely to
offer up a sacrificial lamb – even a member

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.680
of D Class – to anyone else - Well, save
for Dr. Bright’s New Body Quota.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.259
But Doctor Clef has always been capable of
producing results that align with the Foundation’s

00:05:41.259 --> 00:05:44.220
objectives, no matter the cost incurred.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:48.470
Clef has been known to deem any losses, even
the deaths of civilians, to be acceptable

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:52.139
collateral damage in order to kill or contain
anomalies.

00:05:52.139 --> 00:05:57.419
And he’s under no illusions that the Foundation
wouldn’t indulge his erratic behavior if

00:05:57.419 --> 00:05:58.970
not for his track record.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.580
However, no one in the Foundation knew for
certain if Doctor Clef even needed to start

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.120
his day with such gratuitous violence.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.660
As well as being renowned as a killer, Clef
was also a prolific liar.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.680
Were there legitimate reasons for him starting
his day like this?

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.569
Or was it all a front, merely done so he could
continue to promote his self-image as the

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:21.300
Foundation’s most ruthless researcher?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:26.139
The lack of a clear answer was widely considered
to be frustrating to other members of Foundation

00:06:26.139 --> 00:06:27.139
personnel.

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:30.330
12:00 PM
Noon, and after a few hours of tending to

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.460
his duties as the Department Head for the
Division of Training and Development, Clef

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.990
usually takes a prompt lunch break.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:42.270
Every day, as the clock strikes exactly midday,
on the precise hour of twelve o’clock, Doctor

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.550
Alto Clef will stride into the mess hall.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:48.680
There, a number of Foundation researchers
will normally be gathered, eating lunch and

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.240
quietly conversing among themselves.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.680
Popular lunchtime topics of conversation usually
tend to revolve around ways the Foundation

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:02.229
could try to eliminate SCP-682, or what type
of pie is being served in the commissary.

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:06.520
On this particular day, it’s apple pecan,
in case you were wondering.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.300
Naturally, as with many things that Doctor
Clef does, his reasons for taking a trip into

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.110
the mess hall aren’t at all the same as
any normal person’s.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:20.289
That is to say, he doesn’t go there to eat;
or at least, in the conventional sense.

00:07:20.289 --> 00:07:25.389
What Alto Clef does, every lunchtime without
fail, is deliberately and methodically pace

00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:27.650
his way around the mess hall.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:32.889
In his hands is his ukulele, the instrument
from which his various monikers have been

00:07:32.889 --> 00:07:35.620
derived: Ukulele Man, Agent Ukulele.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.449
Even ‘Alto Clef’ is a nickname; the doctor
has always claimed his real name is an A Major

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:45.050
chord played on a ukulele, making it unpronounceable
to humans.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:49.740
With his preferred instrument in hand, Clef
will plod between the tables that eating researchers

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.740
are sitting at.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:55.919
Each step he takes is punctuated by the strum
of a note on his ukulele, as he’ll play

00:07:55.919 --> 00:07:59.419
a random song painfully slowly as he strides
around.

00:07:59.419 --> 00:08:05.000
One lunchtime, it took him an entire two hours
to get through a rendition of Smoke on the

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.960
Water note by agonizing note.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.680
Even though it doesn’t seem to be a meal
in the traditional sense – meaning it offers

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.560
him no nutritional value – Clef professes
that his midday ritual allows him to feed

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.350
on the fear of his fellow researchers.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.990
Seeing him creepily walking around and playing
slow, drawn-out renditions of songs on his

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:29.729
ukulele is occasionally something that intimidates
the newer personnel at the Foundation.

00:08:29.729 --> 00:08:34.430
But anyone who has been there for long enough
just finds it annoying; which might be Clef’s

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:37.610
intention, that or simply fuelling his own
ego.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:41.349
1:30 PM
Usually, by the time an hour and a half have

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:46.060
elapsed from the start of his lunch break,
Alto Clef will reluctantly return to his work.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:50.490
He’ll often proceed over the course of a
mid-afternoon, to conduct research into the

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:54.550
latest reality warping anomaly he has been
tasked with decommissioning for that day.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:59.560
It was during one such time of day that he
came up with his plan for the now-infamous

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.860
SCP-239 Incident.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:06.459
An anomalous girl was recovered by the Foundation,
with the ability to alter reality specifically

00:09:06.459 --> 00:09:09.810
relating to her or her immediate surroundings.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:15.029
Doctor Clef viewed SCP-239 as a threat to
security and that the Foundation repeatedly

00:09:15.029 --> 00:09:19.160
overestimated its ability to contain reality-altering
entities.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:25.350
So, Clef proposed a plan involving a sharp
implement made out of SCP-148, a metal that

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.110
could block certain anomalous properties.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:33.330
Clef even volunteers himself to terminate
SCP-239 personally, and would have succeeded

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.010
had the Foundation not intervened.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:41.010
Most of the plans Doctor Alto Clef devised
usually placed emphasis on eliminating anomalies

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.910
instead of containing them or making them
safe.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:48.640
Additionally, his schemes almost always ended
in a large number of deaths, either of disposable

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.779
D Class personnel or of civilians.

00:09:51.779 --> 00:09:56.830
On this particular day, Doctor Clef has been
tasked with an assignment he found to be particularly

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:59.850
egregious: curing something.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:05.430
Namely, SCP-451, a former Foundation agent
who suffered an accident with an anomalous

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:09.290
artifact that made him unable to perceive
other people around him.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.990
The agent quickly came to the conclusion that
he was the last surviving person on the planet,

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:17.110
and that he was responsible for wiping out
the human race.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:22.680
Naturally, Clef’s proposed solution to this
problem was to simply kill SCP-451.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:26.640
He could still be seen by other Foundation
staff, but nobody could interact with him

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.640
directly.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.800
It was as though the artifact had caused a
reality-warping event focused solely on that

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.960
one agent, shifting him just outside of reality
itself.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:41.670
However, after spending hours brainstorming
a way to decommission SCP-451, another researcher

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:45.149
abruptly reminded Doctor Clef that the agent
could no longer be killed.

00:10:45.149 --> 00:10:49.620
As a result, in a fit of madness, Clef instead
killed that researcher, before continuing

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.329
as if he had been unphased by the information.

00:10:52.329 --> 00:10:55.470
4:00 PM
Despite normally having done barely enough

00:10:55.470 --> 00:11:01.190
work to justify it, at this point in his day
Clef often likes to treat himself to an additional,

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:02.190
unearned, break.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:06.639
As with much of his regular flouting of rules,
he often rationalizes the extra time off with

00:11:06.639 --> 00:11:09.529
the knowledge that he is apparently untouchable.

00:11:09.529 --> 00:11:13.899
Clef knows that there is very little the Foundation
can do to reprimand him, given both his status

00:11:13.899 --> 00:11:19.410
as a high-value researcher and his historical
track record for dealing with anomalies.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:24.519
Simultaneously, he liked to exercise his immunity
to both consequences and the effects of certain

00:11:24.519 --> 00:11:26.060
anomalies.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:30.959
Part of what makes Clef such a valuable asset
to the SCP Foundation is not just his extensive

00:11:30.959 --> 00:11:35.450
knowledge of reality-warpers; although he
is considered perhaps the leading expert in

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.000
such SCPs.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:42.230
But Alto has also been known to negate the
anomalous abilities of some SCPs, rendering

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:45.910
him unaffected in the same way ordinary researchers
are.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:50.690
Much like his fellow long-standing Foundation
scientist Doctor Jack Bright, this has rendered

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:56.300
Clef largely indestructible and unharmable
to a majority of anomalies, allowing him to

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:00.120
continue his tenure at the Foundation for
a considerable time.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.500
As a result of this natural immunity, it is
often during this part of his day that Doctor

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:09.649
Clef likes to pay visits to a former romantic
flame: SCP-173.

00:12:09.649 --> 00:12:15.410
Yes, the Sculpture, the concrete and rebar
anomaly capable of moving at impossible speeds

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.089
when unobserved.

00:12:17.089 --> 00:12:24.540
Doctor Clef and SCP-173 have what you might
call a ‘special bond’, although the Sculpture

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.430
seems somewhat indifferent to him given that
it cannot emote.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:34.360
Clef, however, has been known to be infatuated
with SCP-173, able to view it without being

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:35.360
harmed.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.199
The unlikely couple have even, on a number
of occasions, shared romantic evenings in

00:12:40.199 --> 00:12:41.670
each other’s company.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:46.250
In the dining room of Site-19, listening to
Barry White and enjoying an exquisite meal

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:52.269
prepared by D Class, Clef enjoyed the company
of SCP-173 – the Sculpture wearing a black

00:12:52.269 --> 00:12:54.260
dress and blonde wig.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:57.750
Every week, he looked forward to Friday: their
date night.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.290
7:00 PM
“Okay, let’s see the damage today,”

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:02.290
Doctor Gears sighs.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:05.949
By this point in the day, one of the last
few orders of business on Doctor Clef’s

00:13:05.949 --> 00:13:09.600
itinerary was always his daily, mandatory
reprimand.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.430
Despite there being little punishments that
the Foundation could issue Alto with for both

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:18.730
his annoying and alarming actions, they would
still regularly subject Clef to a list of

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.250
his recent rule violations and casualties.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:26.650
“At the time of 7pm, we’ve logged over
fifty confirmed instances of personnel deaths

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:30.510
on-site,” Doctor Gears reads aloud, rolling
his eyes.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.510
“Only fifty?

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.269
I must be having a slow day!”

00:13:33.269 --> 00:13:34.269
Clef responds.

00:13:34.269 --> 00:13:36.620
“That is, if you’re sure your numbers
are right.”

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:41.240
“Clef, this game of yours doesn’t get
any less tiring,” the other researcher tells

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:42.240
him.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.500
“If you’ve killed anyone else today, please
just cut to the chase and tell me how many.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.360
Oh, and if you think it’s funny to keep
stashing bodies all over the place, then one:

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:51.360
it’s not.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.920
And two: I need to know where those are too.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:14:00.029
Oh, and three: just try, for once, for the
sake of my sanity, to tell the truth.”

00:14:00.029 --> 00:14:02.660
“Oh, Charlie, you’re no fun!”

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.220
Doctor Clef replies with a chuckle.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.110
“This is fun to you?”

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.279
Gears asks.

00:14:07.279 --> 00:14:08.279
“This?

00:14:08.279 --> 00:14:09.279
Right here, right now?

00:14:09.279 --> 00:14:11.079
Of course not, you know me better than that!

00:14:11.079 --> 00:14:16.160
Look, we both know the reasons that the folks
upstairs get you to sit me down, give me a

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.160
scolding.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:20.360
It’s all a front, just a way to stop any
of those other little researchers getting

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.850
any big ideas.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:24.910
The Council can’t bear the thought of anyone
else trying to do as I do.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:29.340
There’s only one Doctor Clef, and we both
know there’s nothing anyone in the whole

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.860
Foundation can do to stop me having fun.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.579
My numbers are too good.”

00:14:34.579 --> 00:14:37.370
“Speaking of your numbers,” Gears ignores
him.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.390
“It says here you’ve received…

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.600
four-hundred and twenty complaints about the
ukulele playing.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:49.620
You want to cut to the chase and tell me how
many of these were filed by you as pranks?”

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:53.230
“Aw, Charlie, you do know me!”

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.630
8:00 PM
As very often happens around the time that

00:14:56.630 --> 00:15:01.560
most personnel have punched their cards for
the day, Doctor Clef is approached by a trembling

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.430
researcher, trying hard to hide the fear on
their face.

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:09.570
While starting as a more intermittent occurrence,
encounters like this have become so frequent

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:13.840
that they have since come to form a regular
part of Clef’s daily routine.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.839
“I’m on to you, Clef!”

00:15:15.839 --> 00:15:17.070
the researcher said nervously.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:21.050
They were the latest in a long, long line
of Foundation staff to confront Doctor Clef

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.579
about his supposed ‘true nature’.

00:15:23.579 --> 00:15:27.709
Given his violent and unpredictable behavior,
there were rampant rumors that there was more

00:15:27.709 --> 00:15:29.339
to him than it first seemed.

00:15:29.339 --> 00:15:31.579
“Come on then, kid,” he says.

00:15:31.579 --> 00:15:35.260
“I haven’t got all night, let’s hear
what you think you’ve got.”

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:39.399
“You were with the Global Occult Coalition,
before you defected to the Foundation,”

00:15:39.399 --> 00:15:43.389
the researcher declared, summoning up more
courage, even if it was a façade.

00:15:43.389 --> 00:15:48.240
“You wrote their handbook on reality benders,
but nobody in the world could have that much

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.829
knowledge about anomalies like that… unless
they were also one.”

00:15:51.829 --> 00:15:53.829
“Ooh, spooky!”

00:15:53.829 --> 00:15:56.440
Doctor Clef taunts, inching closer with his
ukulele in one hand.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.850
“The Foundation literally let you get away
with murder, your face can’t be photographed

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.560
without changing the image into grinning animals,
you’re-you’re…”

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.040
“Go on, you can do it!”

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.040
Clef urges.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.040
“You’re an anomaly.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.040
An SCP.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:12.790
You’ve broken out of containment, and you’re
warping reality to avoid detection!”

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.390
the researcher blurts out, adding “You’re
the Devil!”

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.300
“Oh, I’m disappointed!”

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:20.389
Clef chortles, finding the theory amusing.

00:16:20.389 --> 00:16:24.120
“You almost stuck the landing, why throw
in something so unoriginal?

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.980
Let me ask you, do you honestly think you’re
the first?

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:33.079
The only one in the Foundation to ‘connect
all the dots’ and figure out the truth behind

00:16:33.079 --> 00:16:34.180
Alto Clef?

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.180
You aren’t.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:40.769
If I was an anomaly… or the Devil, aren’t
I being a little too obvious about it?”

00:16:40.769 --> 00:16:45.540
With a clunk of a ukulele against the researcher’s
head, Clef gets one more decommissioning in

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.359
before bedtime.

00:16:47.359 --> 00:16:51.890
Perhaps there is some truth to what he says,
maybe his power isn't just his immortality

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:55.160
or combat prowess, or immunity to anomalies.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:17:00.060
It could be how he’s been able to influence
everyone’s perception of him, even manipulating

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:03.699
the O5 Council into thinking he's too big
of a threat.

00:17:03.699 --> 00:17:09.419
His actions have made them believe that Doctor
Clef is better kept on-side as an asset than

00:17:09.419 --> 00:17:12.780
to roam free as a dangerous enemy to the Foundation.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.620
That could be what he wants them all to think,
even if it’s not true.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:22.500
After all, Alto Clef is a notorious liar;
his entire persona could be the ultimate lie.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:26.069
10:00 PM
After another day of murder and mayhem – mostly

00:17:26.069 --> 00:17:30.570
of his own doing – Doctor Alto Clef returns
to his quarters long after the working day

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.270
is officially over.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:36.500
After disposing of the evidence of his latest
‘decommissioning’, he makes his way back

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:41.110
to the room he started the day in, and will
start the next one in too.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:44.559
But if you think that Clef just gets into
pyjamas, hops into bed, and has a full eight

00:17:44.559 --> 00:17:49.030
hours of sleep like a normal person, then
you’d be way, way off.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:54.230
Firstly, on his way back to his room, Clef
will once again have his ukulele with him,

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:57.830
sinisterly strumming away at the strings so
everyone knows, as they try to sleep in their

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.549
own quarters, that he’s still awake.

00:18:00.549 --> 00:18:06.320
What’s worse is at this time of night, Alto
intentionally mistunes his instrument, making

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:10.830
it all the more egregious to hear, keeping
the other researchers up until he finally

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:13.220
makes it back to his own quarters.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:18.180
You might think he would have the sense to
stop there, but he doesn’t, still discordantly

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:23.520
and tunelessly plucking at the strings, usually
until someone dares to gather up the bravery

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.360
to complain about the noise.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:31.460
All of it is to add fuel to the fire of his
reputation, his image as an unhinged, unreasonable

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.620
and untrustworthy force.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:37.780
His behavior is all carefully curated and
performed with the intention to make the rest

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:41.240
of the Foundation believe there is something
off about him.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.240
And why?

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:47.470
Well, if they’re so focused on the strange
things they can see and hear Doctor Clef doing,

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:52.420
it provides a smokescreen that covers up his
true goals, all the dark and twisted things

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.740
he is truly capable.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:59.419
And if killing anomalies and personnel is
his cover, one can only imagine what might

00:18:59.419 --> 00:19:01.240
be worse than that.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:05.600
Much in the same vein, even him retreating
to his quarters at the end of the day is designed

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.610
to get in the heads of the rest of the Foundation.

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:13.320
Maybe because Clef really is the Devil, or
a reality-warping SCP.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:18.520
Or perhaps he just enjoys messing with people,
making them think he’s going to sleep.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:23.370
Not one of them knows that he’s actually
laying in bed, eyes fixed open as wide as

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.370
possible…

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.090
with his face locked in that signature grin.

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:32.200
Now go and check out “DR CLEF SCP FOUNDATION
RESEARCHER” and “A DAY IN THE LIFE OF

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.650
SCP-049” for more deep dives on Foundation
favorites!

